@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api/students

### 1. Add Student 1 (Excellent - Stronger in Programming)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentId": "S101",
  "studentName": "Aarav Sharma",
  "email": "aarav@example.com",
  "courseName": "CSE",
  "programmingScore": 92.0,
  "mathematicsScore": 88.0,
  "technicalSkills": ["Java", "Spring Boot", "MySQL"]
}

### 2. Add Student 2 (Weak in Programming < 50, Strong in Math >= 75)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentId": "S102",
  "studentName": "Priya Verma",
  "email": "priya@example.com",
  "courseName": "CSEAI",
  "programmingScore": 42.0,
  "mathematicsScore": 84.0,
  "technicalSkills": ["Python", "Java"]
}

### 3. Add Student 3 (Good - Equal Scores)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentId": "S103",
  "studentName": "Rohan Gupta",
  "email": "rohan@example.com",
  "courseName": "CSE",
  "programmingScore": 76.0,
  "mathematicsScore": 76.0,
  "technicalSkills": ["MySQL", "React"]
}

### 4. Test Validation: Duplicate Student ID (Should return 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentId": "S101",
  "studentName": "Duplicate User",
  "email": "dup@example.com",
  "courseName": "IT",
  "programmingScore": 80.0,
  "mathematicsScore": 80.0,
  "technicalSkills": ["C++"]
}

### 5. Test Validation: Invalid Score > 100 (Should return 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentId": "S104",
  "studentName": "Invalid Score User",
  "email": "invalid@example.com",
  "courseName": "IT",
  "programmingScore": 105.0,
  "mathematicsScore": 70.0,
  "technicalSkills": ["Java"]
}

### 6. Retrieve All Students
GET {{baseUrl}}

### 7. Search Student by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/S101

### 8. Search Student by Email
GET {{baseUrl}}/search/email?email=priya@example.com

### 9. Search Students by Course
GET {{baseUrl}}/search/course?course=CSE

### 10. Display Merit List (Sorted by Average Score Descending)
GET {{baseUrl}}/merit-list

### 11. Identify Students with Same Technical Skills
GET {{baseUrl}}/shared-skills

### 12. Display Weak Programming (< 50) & Strong Math (>= 75) Students
GET {{baseUrl}}/weak-programming-strong-math

### 13. Update Student Scores and Skills
PUT {{baseUrl}}/S102
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "programmingScore": 78.0,
  "mathematicsScore": 85.0,
  "technicalSkills": ["Python", "Java", "Docker"]
}

### 14. Delete a Student Record
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/S101